#Short README
# See the attached journal article
# Dangi, N., Sodja, J., & Yu, W. (2025). Divergence‐Free Correction for Synthetic Wind Fields. Wind Energy, 28(11), e70062.


# Scripts for performing Helmholtz-Hodge decomposition in three ways: 
1. FFT (Fourier transform based) -> ready to run script placed
2. FFT based but constrained to user specified bounds -> ready to run script placed
3. Matrix discretisation -> partially ready to run script placed with all calculation functions. It is advised to run it with 32-64GB+ RAM, from personal experience
#  "runscript_*.m" for performing the correction that takes in data from "Data" folder
  #creates "*_divfree*" folders to save divergence free wind fields

# Short comparison
1. FFT based-> Uses significantly less RAM; but, assumes periodicity and if not, uses mirror techniques
2. Matrix based -> More accurate given the less strict assumptions on underlying data; but, significantly more expensive due to the matrix inversion
3. FFT constrained-> same as 1 but allows to limit changes to several statistics of the wind fields

# Inputs
1. TurbSim style ".wnd" files-> can easily be changed to take in ".bts" files too

# Outputs
1. Divergence‐Free wind Fields

#  example post-processing scripts placed as "postP*.m" files 
  #creates "Images" folder
# Sample inputs of wind field of two different coherence models are placed for one of the operating conditions
# These are "R NABL Diff Decay" and "R NABL Kaimal Decay" as detailed in the attached article

# Currently "Images" and "*_divfree*" folders are already populated. You may rerun the scripts and overwrite or copy current ouptuts as example outputs
